{"additions":3238,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Closes #177\n\n## What\n\nThe GitHub page's issue and PR lists now keep themselves current without spending API points.\n\n- Every `github-poll-interval` (scaled by the idle / low-quota rules from #168, off with `github-auto-refresh \"off\"`) the page sends **one conditional REST request** for the repository's most recently updated issue or PR: `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues?state=all&sort=updated&direction=desc&per_page=1` with `If-None-Match: <etag>`.\n- A `304 Not Modified` answer costs nothing against the quota (verified with `gh api -i`). Only when the ETag / `updated_at` moves does vig re-fetch both lists and the open issue / PR detail.\n- The first `200` is only a baseline (no refetch); later answers compare against it.\n- Status bar: `lists 12s ago` (age of the lists) and a short green `↻ updated` after a change-driven refresh.\n\n## Fixtures\n\n- `vig fixtures record` now starts from an empty directory so the set is exactly the recording (stale run / log fixtures were piling up), records the change check, and keeps only its status line, `Etag` and body — the other response headers describe the recording account (OAuth scopes, request ids) and must not be checked in.\n- Under `VIG_GH_FIXTURE` replay the check is sent unconditionally, so the single recorded `200` answers every tick.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `change_check_parses_304_and_200` (client): status line / ETag / body parsing.\n- `change_check_baseline_then_change_refetches_lists` (state): baseline → same watermark → moved watermark; only the last one re-fetches and shows the notice.\n\n## Docs\n\nGuide (`views-github`, `config-reference` → `github-poll-interval`) en / ja, README en / ja.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":51,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-09T07:37:10Z","deletions":4868,"headRefName":"feat/github-list-autorefresh","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":179,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMwmBJw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere are confirmed correctness/reliability issues in the change-check parsing and in how list refresh timestamps and fixture recording errors are handled.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds a low-cost auto-refresh mechanism to the GitHub page so Issue/PR lists stay current without consuming GraphQL quota, using a conditional REST change check and surfacing list freshness in the status bar. Updates the fixtures recorder and documentation to cover the new polling behavior.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add a periodic conditional `gh api -i` change check (ETag/`updated_at`) to trigger Issue/PR list refreshes only when something changes.\n- Show list freshness (`lists … ago`) and a brief `↻ updated` notice in the GitHub status bar after change-driven refreshes.\n- Record and sanitize the new change-check fixture output; refresh fixture outputs accordingly; update docs (en/ja).\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/github/state.rs | Tracks list watermark/refresh times and triggers refresh on change-check results. |\r\n| src/github/domain/client.rs | Implements the conditional REST change check and parsing of `gh api -i` output. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Renders `lists …` age and `↻ updated` flash in the GitHub status bar. |\r\n| src/fixtures.rs | Records the new change check and trims sensitive/unneeded headers from its fixture. |\r\n| README.md | Documents the new change-driven list auto-refresh behavior. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README update describing change-driven list auto-refresh. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-github.md | Documents list auto-refresh behavior and status bar indicators. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-github.md | Japanese guide update for list auto-refresh behavior and indicators. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-reference.md | Expands `github-poll-interval` description to include list change checks. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md | Japanese config reference update for the same. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_-i_repos_owner_repo_issues_state_all_sort_updated_direction_desc_per_page_1.out | New recorded fixture for the REST change check (`gh api -i …/issues?…per_page=1`). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_list_--json_number_title_state_author_labels_createdAt_parent_--limit_50.out | Fixture updated to reflect current issues list state. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/pr_list_--json_number_title_state_author_labels_headRefName_baseRefName_createdAt_reviewDecision_isDraft_--limit_50.out | Fixture updated to reflect current PR list state. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-pr-stacks_-F_owner_td72_-F_name_vig_-F_first_50.out | Fixture updated to reflect current PR stacks query result. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-meta_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2.out | Fixture updated (rateLimit remaining changed). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-items_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2_-F_first_8.out | Fixture updated (rateLimit remaining changed). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_list_--limit_50_--json_databaseId_number_name_workflowName_status_conclusion_headBranch_event_createdAt_updatedAt_url.out | Workflow runs list fixture refreshed to newer run set. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_177_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | New fixture for issue #177. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_178_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | New fixture for issue #178. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_170_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Removed/updated fixture no longer present in the refreshed fixture set. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/pr_view_174_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_reviews_labels_createdAt_reviewDecision_statusCheckRollup_additions_deletions_changedFiles.out | Removed/updated fixture no longer present in the refreshed fixture set. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34321905536_--json_jobs.out | New/updated jobs fixture for run 34321905536. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34321905536_--log_--job_102370223944.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34321905536. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34321905536_--log_--job_102370251106.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34321905536. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34321905536_--log_--job_102370255132.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34321905536. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34321905372_--json_jobs.out | New/updated jobs fixture for run 34321905372. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34234443135_--json_jobs.out | New/updated jobs fixture for run 34234443135. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34234443135_--log_--job_102088424304.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34234443135. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34234443135_--log_--job_102088425270.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34234443135. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34234443135_--log_--job_102088468235.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34234443135. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34215031954_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34215031954_--log_--job_102024676255.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34215031954. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34215031954_--log_--job_102024676869.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34215031954. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34215031954_--log_--job_102024719398.out | New/updated job log fixture for run 34215031954. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34214691158_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34214640237_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34214267144_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34214261508_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34214261426_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161906_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161726_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161710_--json_jobs.out | Removed/updated jobs fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161710_--log_--job_102018647351.out | Removed/updated job log fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34213161710_--log_--job_102018699684.out | Removed/updated job log fixture (no longer present after refresh). |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/fixtures.rs:46**\n* Ignoring errors from `list_pr_stacks` can leave the fixture set incomplete (missing the recorded response), which will later fail in replay mode when the GitHub page tries to load PR stacks. Treat this fetch as required during recording so fixture refresh fails loudly and deterministically.\n```\n    step(\"pull requests + stacks\");\n    let prs = gh::list_prs(50).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n    let _ = gh::list_pr_stacks(50);\n    for p in &prs {\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 37/51 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-09T07:42:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d8133819eab19a9b837d55207d786090922809b5"}}],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-09T07:41:37Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34324764354/job/102379374210","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-09T07:37:18Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-09T07:37:56Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34324764269/job/102379373848","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-09T07:37:18Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-09T07:40:27Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34324764354/job/102379373989","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-09-09T07:37:20Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-09T07:43:17Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34324764354/job/102379374313","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-09T07:37:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-09T07:43:17Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34324764354/job/102381054633","name":"upload","s